<BaseLayout title="SharedID — First-Party Identity & Privacy Platform (Prebid)">
  <section id="sharedid-case-study" class="case-study">
  <h2>SharedID – Publisher-Controlled Identity at Scale</h2>
  <p class="case-study-summary">
    SharedID enabled a <strong>publisher-controlled, privacy-aware identity framework</strong> that reduced fragmentation
    across the programmatic ecosystem and prepared publishers for a cookieless future.
    The initiative combined <strong>platform strategy, ecosystem collaboration, and standards leadership</strong>
    to deliver a scalable identity solution adopted across the open web.
  </p>


  <h3>Strategic Challenge</h3>
  <p>
    Publishers faced fragmented and inconsistent identity signals across the header bidding ecosystem as browsers restricted third-party cookies.
    This made it harder for buyers to match users and for publishers to maximize yield across partners.
  </p>
  <p>
    The opportunity was to develop a <strong>consistent, publisher-controlled user identity</strong> that could be stored in
    <strong>first-party context</strong>, reduce reliance on third-party cookie syncing, and provide a common namespace across ecosystem participants.
    Successfully addressing this required balancing <strong>privacy, interoperability, and publisher control</strong>.
  </p>

  <h3>My Role & Leadership</h3>
  <p>
    I led the product strategy for integrating SharedID into our platform, aligning internal teams and external partners on a
    vision of <strong>publisher-first identity at scale</strong>. I defined the product roadmap, prioritized capabilities that balanced
    performance and privacy, and coordinated cross-functional collaboration with ecosystem stakeholders.
  </p>

  <h3>Impact & Outcomes</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Enabled a <strong>publisher-controlled universal identifier</strong> that reduced reliance on fragmented third-party signals
      and cookie syncing across header bidding partners.
    <li>
      Increased identity consistency for participating partners, improving <strong>user match rates and bid relevance</strong>
      within programmatic auctions. 
    </li>
    <li>
      Supported publisher readiness for a <strong>cookieless future</strong> by leveraging first-party storage mechanisms while honoring
      consent and privacy preferences. 
    </li>
    <li>
      Advanced industry adoption of an open, community-owned solution, strengthening the role of the open web vs.
      proprietary alternatives. 
  </ul>

  <h3>Takeaway</h3>
  <p>
    SharedID showcases how strategic product leadership can unlock open, scalable identity solutions that empower publishers,
    improve ecosystem collaboration, and prepare platforms for a privacy-centric future.
  </p>
</section>


</BaseLayout>
